blocks.body:
A number line is a straight line with:

1. a mark labelled 0 (OpenStax calls it the origin);
2. more marks, called tick marks, all the same distance apart (one unit);
3. the numbers 1, 2, 3, ... written at the marks, in order, getting bigger to the right.

A dot on the line is called a point. A point at a mark stands for that number: the point at 4 is 4 units from 0. OpenStax says the number is the coordinate of the point.
